WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.250
Your bike seems to be okay.

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.580
Let's start together.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.940
She's right.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.400
Fuyune-chan?

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.530
Do you think we're that heartless?

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.870
Is everyone ready?

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.200
Yeah.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.330
Yes.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.210
I'm ready any time.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:24.790
Here we go.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.060
<b>#7  What Can I Do?</b>

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.060
<i>The Minami Kamakura Night 
Criterium has finally started.</i>

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.780
<i>Currently, a fierce race between the 
beginners is taking place on the track.</i>

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:20.240
<i>Leading the race is the first-year pack 
headed by the cosplay club's Mr. Bear.</i>

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.200
<i>Following behind them 
is the second-year pack.</i>

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.160
<i>Behind them are the third-years
 and the bicycle club.</i>

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:33.090
<i>Will they be able to catch up?</i>

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.050
You can do it, bicycle club!

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.090
Go!

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.400
We can't see them anymore.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.930
They are riding road racers.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.410
It can't be helped. We can't 
chase them around the whole time.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.150
Leave that to me.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.750
Sabaya-san?

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.820
This criterium is being broadcast 
by Ototo Electronics.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.820
<b>Electronics</b>

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.280
And this is the secret weapon of the day...

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.750
A quadcopter designed 
for aerial photography!

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.540
Not bad, Sabaya-san.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:15.150
This is nothing.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.300
Quit bragging and show us 
the bicycle club already!

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.420
R-Roger that!

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.570
Stare...

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.570
So much pressure...

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:29.110
Hurry up. Have you found them yet?

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.170
I found them!

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:34.310
They're here.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:38.700
Where are the people riding in front of us?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.810
We haven't seen anyone for a while.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.660
They're probably on the opposite 
side of the martial arts gym.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.620
If we don't catch them soon, 
the race will be over.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:50.910
But if we ride as hard as we can now,
we won't make it until the end.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.950
We'll never catch up with that attitude.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.780
What? What are we supposed to do, then?

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.970
<i>Fuyune-san's right. We have to attack.</i>

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.510
I'll ride in front. Follow me.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:07.710
What?

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.820
Start by getting used to the pace and track.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.770
I'll lead the group until then.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.140
You're right. That could work.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.680
We're counting on you, Natsumi.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:17.400
Thanks.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.900
Here we go.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:26.980
<i>What is that?</i>

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.000
<i>There's trouble on the track.</i>

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.240
<i>A group of second-years have gotten 
tangled and are stopped on the course.</i>

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:38.450
<i>It seems they collided when they entered a 
corner without making way for each other.</i>

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.830
What are they, idiots?

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.860
The next group of riders are coming!

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.670
Clear the track!

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.300
They're quicker than I expected.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.440
Hiroko, we should hurry.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.560
Hold on.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.270
Coming through!

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.520
Azuma-senpai...

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.360
You can do it.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.040
Why did you let them pass us?

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.600
Isn't it obvious?

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.950
It's more fun to pass people from behind.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.980
Why did I feel a sudden chill?

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.160
Guys.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.940
We're in the straight before the finish line.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.870
<i>While the second-years were 
experience difficulties,</i>

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:18.450
<i>the bicycle club, which had a slow start,
became the second group to enter the straight</i>

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.860
<i>before the finish line 
after the first-year pack.</i>

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.090
Go, Sis!

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.710
<i>Do you girls know what you're doing?</i>

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:30.340
<i>How you handle this long straight will 
be an important part of the race.</i>

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.850
Guys, do you remember Shiki-sensei's advice?

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.980
Uh, what did she say?

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.530
It was that.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.450
The one where we ride in single file.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:42.590
Oh, right.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:44.230
Wind resistance?

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.350
That's right.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:50.200
Doesn't the wind sometimes feel like 
a wall when you're riding your bike?

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.560
You're right.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:56.330
The faster you try to ride, the more 
it feels like you're riding underwater.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:58.600
That's wind resistance.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.540
It's a cyclist's greatest enemy.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.820
When you ride alone, you bear 
the brunt of its effects.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.260
But it's a different story 
if you're riding in a group.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.950
Since the leader pushes 
the wall of air aside,

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.220
the members riding behind 
them have an easier time.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.230
You can beat the wind by riding as 
a group in what's known as...

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:18.490
<i>...a train!</i>

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.150
Ride in single file...

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:27.780
I'm going to crash.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.320
Maiharu-san...

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:31.730
You don't need to force 
yourself to stay that close.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:35.320
Since it's our first train,
let's leave some space between us.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:37.580
It should still be effective.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.500
O-Okay!

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.880
<i>This is amazing. I can't believe 
the wind resistance disappeared.</i>

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.640
<i>This is a train.</i>

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.060
<i>I don't really understand it, 
but it seems to be working.</i>

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.120
What's going on? They're so fast.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.220
Are their bikes that much better than ours?

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.020
Mikako, let's raise our speed.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:08.890
You were right, Hiroko.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:12.280
Catching up and passing someone does 
make the race more interesting.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.280
Let's go, Mikako!

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:14.870
Sure thing!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.330
Let's win this race!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.880
<i>The race is entering its third lap.</i>

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:22.330
<b>Lap 3/8 Laps Remain</b>

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:22.330
<b>1. #108/Bear/Cosplay Club
2. #111/Arakura Arisa/Basketball Team
3. #115/Inoue Eri/Track Team</b>

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.330
<i>Leading the race is the first-year pack.</i>

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.170
<i>The bicycle club is catching up 
to them by riding close together.</i>

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:30.310
<i>The second-years following them 
have become completely scattered.</i>

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:31.940
<i>There are eight laps remaining.</i>

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:35.510
<i>What kind of developments await us?</i>

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.880
Keep it up, everyone.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.270
Think of Shiki-sensei's 
other piece of advice.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:44.350
Her other piece of advice? I think it was...

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.360
Turn your pedals instead of stepping on them.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.860
Turn them?

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.240
Isn't it obvious?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:58.550
Are you sure? What do you do when you 
try to ride quickly or climb hills?

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.300
I step on them as hard as I can.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.500
Stand and pedal?

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:06.990
Those do work for immediately 
increasing your speed,

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:10.340
but ultimately you'll be able to 
keep up your strength for longer

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:15.490
by imaging yourself rotating your pedals.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.600
Turn instead of stepping...

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:26.150
Their pedaling is passable. It's pretty 
good since they just started training.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:29.820
They're not bad for a group of beginners.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.360
It's because they're beginners.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:31.860
What?

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.070
No one's good at anything 
right when they start.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:40.350
But because they're not good, 
they want to get better.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:46.250
I'm sure they'll make a lot of mistakes, 
but by going all out to face a challenge,

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:50.050
they'll learn their limits and expand 
their skills little by little.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:53.350
And that's tons of fun.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:54.390
You're right.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.870
They're creating a pleasant breeze.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.640
Maybe so, but...

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:08.730
<b>Lap 3/8 Laps Remain</b>

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:08.730
<b>1. #108/Bear/Cosplay Club
2. #115/Inoue Eri/Track Team
3. #111/Arakura Arisa/Basketball Team</b>

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:08.730
I'm curious about the pack maintaining
its distance in front of the cycling club.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.560
The third-years, huh?

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.360
They're kind of creepy, aren't they?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.830
The three girls in front are creating a wall

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.360
to reduce the burden on 
the girls behind them.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.450
But I didn't realize our school had

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.580
<b>Lap 3/8 Laps Remain</b>

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.580
<b>1. #108/Bear/Cosplay Club
2. #115/Inoue Eri/Track Team
3. #111/Arakura Arisa/Basketball Team</b>

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.580
any students who knew enough 
about bicycles to do that.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.040
Maybe someone taught them.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.360
That was me.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.400
What?

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.310
M-Manager?

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:35.530
They were generous enough to buy 
yakisoba and omelets from me,

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:36.680
so I thanked them by telling them.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.750
You shouldn't be teaching the enemy anything 
that would give them an advantage.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.390
Don't worry.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:46.850
The third-years aren't the only ones 
who generously bought my products.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:48.810
It's so good!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.750
It's generously topped with fresh 
locally-produced whitebait and

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.770
overflowing with beef tendon 
mixed with rich egg.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:57.230
This whitebait and tendon omelet 
is something to be feared.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.460
Maiharu-chan really seemed 
to be enjoying her food,

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.010
so I taught her something special.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.000
Something special?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.050
That's right. The long straights 
on today's course stand out,

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:10.710
but there are actually a lot of turns.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.630
How you handle these turns is 
another major part of this race.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.840
Reduce your speed before entering a turn.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.330
Start on the outside and ride 
toward the inside of the turn,

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:23.850
then towards the outside again.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.740
As you exit the turn, accelerate.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:30.140
Those are the slow in, fast 
out and out-in-out techniques.

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:32.020
They're fundamental techniques 
for rounding corners.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:37.290
I see. I did think their cornering was 
surprisingly clean for their first race.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.750
It's because of your hint.

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.990
What do you mean by hint? It was 
a pertinent piece of advice!

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.880
Lap six. The race is already halfway over.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:57.610
We can't make Natsumi pull us the whole way.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:01.890
You're right. We should repay 
her for what she did for us.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.600
Akizuki-san, in front of you!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:04.100
What?

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:06.970
Oh, no!

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:13.310
W-We made it...

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:17.840
That was close. We almost 
charged into the cushions.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.010
Sorry, guys. Should I go slower?

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:25.070
We're fine. I think I'm starting to understand 
what the manager was talking about.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:26.990
I'll do better next time.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.660
Besides, I don't think we 
can afford to go slower.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.830
Azuma-senpai!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.940
<i>While the bicycle club was 
slowed down by the corner,</i>

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.550
<i>the leading second-years closed the gap.</i>

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:42.110
Higa-san, you don't need to go any slower.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:45.900
Instead, follow the path you think is best.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:48.370
We'll trace along your path.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.470
O-Okay.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:52.320
And Fuyune-san, I could use your help.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:53.690
What? Who, me?

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:58.860
Yeah. You said you were confident 
in your memory, right?

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.310
<i>We're entering the middle of the race.</i>

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:04.870
<i>The first-years are still in the lead.</i>

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.700
<i>Behind them are the bicycle club,
riding single file.</i>

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.790
<i>They're quickly catching up.</i>

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:13.920
<i>Will they be able to catch 
up to the lead pack?</i>

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:23.130
The bicycle club really is fast.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.590
At this rate, they'll catch up to us.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:25.630
Bear....

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:27.820
Bear!

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:28.560
Mr. Bear!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.390
Bear, bear, bear, bear, bear, bear!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.400
Bear!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:34.350
<i>The cosplay club's
Mr. Bear is bursting ahead.</i>

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.990
Go!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.560
<i>Is he trying to stay ahead of 
them for the remaining four laps?</i>

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.560
<b>Cosplay Club</b>

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.560
Do whatever it takes to reopen the club!

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.460
Who are they? They seem awfully excited.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.250
That's the cosplay club.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:45.540
They're supposed to be forbidden from 
participating in outside events.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:48.030
Is it okay for them to be 
participating in this race?

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:53.040
Well, since the event's taking place 
on school grounds, I guess it's okay.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:56.540
<i>What's this? The third-years 
are making their move, too.</i>

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:00.050
<i>A group of third-years who have been 
conserving their strength until now</i>

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.800
<i>have charged ahead and are using 
the fallen second-years to</i>

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.550
<i>block the wind as they continue to move up.</i>

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:08.480
<i>It's like they're switching 
trains one after another.</i>

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:11.890
<i>If they keep up this pace, they'll catch 
up to the lead pack before the finish line.</i>

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.600
<i>Things are starting to get interesting.</i>

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:17.070
<i>The next turn is the third.</i>

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.230
Brake at the first cone on the right.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.670
Start turning in the middle of the second.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:32.070
Accelerate after passing 
the light on the left.

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:33.370
Well, Fuyune-san?

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.830
Think you can remember Natsumi-san's path?

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:38.280
This is easy.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:42.700
Bear, bear, bear, bear, bear!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.550
Mr. Bear keeps getting smaller.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.680
We can't catch up to him now.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.930
You can do it, first-years!

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.640
It's the bicycle club.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:55.640
Looks like the first-years 
have met up with each other.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:56.910
Looks like it.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.310
What should we do?
Speed up and catch up to them?

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.570
We still have three more laps.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.470
Instead of pushing ourselves, we should 
close the gap a little at a time.

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:07.280
We caught up to the second-year leaders.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.110
The third-years?

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.480
When did they get here?

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:14.450
You're our next stop.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.660
<b>Lap 7/4 Laps Remain</b>

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.660
<b>1. #108/Bear/Cosplay Club
2. #105/Higa Natsumi/Bicycle Club
3. #102/Maiharu Hiromi/Bicycle Club</b>

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:20.130
<b>Lap 7/4 Laps Remain</b>

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:20.130
<b>1. #108/Bear/Cosplay Club
2. #105/Higa Natsumi/Bicycle Club
3. #102/Maiharu Hiromi/Bicycle Club</b>

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.130
The following pack is moving 
better than I expected.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:23.480
I hope their legs last for three more laps.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:27.090
They've come this far. We just have 
to trust in their teamwork now.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:32.240
<i>Azuma-senpai and the 
third-years are catching up.</i>

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.270
<i>At this rate, we won't be able to stay 
ahead of them until the finish line.</i>

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.140
Girls, do you still have some strength left?

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:39.310
Yeah.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.520
A little.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:45.530
Then stick close behind us. 
Fuyune-san, tell them what to do.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.400
Leave it to me.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.000
Brake now!

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:56.410
Match the person in front 
of you and lean your bike!

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:57.730
Now accelerate!

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:03.940
<i>Fuyune-chan is amazing.</i>

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:08.010
<i>Natsumi-chan's been pulling 
us this whole time, too.</i>

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:13.550
<i>I need to do something, but what can I do?</i>

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.220
<i>What can I do right now?</i>

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:20.710
<i>The lead rider has crossed the 
gate and entered their ninth lap.</i>

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.290
Only two kilometers remain 
until the finish line.

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:26.670
What have you thought of 
the race so far, Principal?

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:27.860
Let's see...

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:32.040
I still don't know who will win.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.240
But no matter how it turns out,

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:38.240
<i>as long as you feel you 
gave everything you had,</i>

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:42.440
<i>I'm sure this will be a fantastic memory.</i>

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.500
<i>There's only one thing I can say to them now.</i>

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:50.130
<i>"Do the very best you can." That's all.</i>

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:57.790
Two more laps. I need to 
catch up to Mr. Bear somehow.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.980
Natsumi-chan, is something wrong?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.400
It's nothing.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.860
<i>This isn't good. It's starting to hurt.</i>

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:13.640
<i>Two more laps.</i>

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.570
<i>I'm okay. I can make it.</i>

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:21.250
God, they're annoying.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:25.130
They're using us to block the wind 
as they recover their strength.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.340
What should we do, Hiroko?

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.870
If they keep following us, 
it'll mean trouble later.

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:34.090
Yeah. We need to get rid of them somewhere 
before we catch up to the bicycle club.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.790
Fuyune-san, are you okay?

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:41.850
J-Just barely. My legs 
haven't cramped up yet.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.270
Really? Then I have an idea.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.190
Will you girls help us, too?

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:51.690
What?

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:56.130
At this rate, the people behind us will 
catch up, and none of us will place first.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:17:00.990
So we should bet on a strategy that'll give 
at least one of us a chance at winning.

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:06.370
We don't want the race to end like this.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.440
We don't know what you're planning...

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:12.500
But if there's anything 
we can do, we'll help.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:14.340
Thanks.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.520
Now!

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.560
The rocket club is on the move!

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:36.450
What? What are you doing?

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.660
Hiromi, Higa-san! Follow us!

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:43.110
From here on out,
we'll pull as hard as we can.

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:44.970
As hard as you can?

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:47.420
What happens when you run out of strength?

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:50.670
Then we'll break away from the group.

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:51.920
No!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:56.950
It's like a rocket.
Expended boosters are discarded.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:02.390
Don't worry. We'll get you 
two in orbit, no matter what.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.940
What are you talking about?

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:05.520
Let's reach the finish line together!

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:10.310
Unfortunately, our legs 
are nearing their limit.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:13.530
This is the only way the 
bicycle club can win.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:17.840
We'll entrust all our 
remaining strength to you.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:21.240
It's our best option right now.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.450
Maiharu-san...

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.400
Let's do it, Maiharu-san.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:28.410
Natsumi-chan...

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.200
We'll never reach the front at this rate.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.580
Let's borrow their strength.

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:37.370
Okay, fine.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.010
Please, girls!

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:42.420
Take us to Mr. Bear!

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:44.970
Bear!

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.340
Here we go, rocket club!

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:48.640
Yeah!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.050
How did they go so far ahead?

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:00.500
The bicycle club is attacking.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.950
Hiroko, it's now or never.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:03.530
Yeah.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.710
First rider breaking away.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:14.450
The rest is up to you.

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:15.700
You can count on us.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.830
Good luck, bicycle club.

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:22.390
Th-Thanks.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.810
<i>They're creating a path for us.</i>

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:41.990
<i>Tomo-chan and Fuyune-chan are 
doing everything they can, too.</i>

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:44.340
<i>What about me?</i>

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:46.500
<i>What can I do?</i>

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:51.750
<i>What can I do?</i>

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.380
<i>No, what do I have to do?</i>

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.160
<i>It's...</i>

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:40.240
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:43.200
<i>A-O-P: The first cycling club.</i>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Choose the frame</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Choose the size</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Accidents (Flats)</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Accidents (Chain)</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Must-have items</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Useful items</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Maintenance</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:48.180
<b>Proper posture</b>

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:48.550
<i>In this segment, we bring you must-see 
information for newbies to road bikes</i>

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:53.890
<b>Fukuo Yui</b>

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:53.890
<b>Hirose Yuki</b>

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:50.760
<i>with A-O-P's Hirose Yuki...</i>

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:52.950
<i>And Fukuo Yui.</i>

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:58.090
<i>No matter how good your bike is, there 
are some things you can't neglect.</i>

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:01.610
<i>"Huh? There's no air!"</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.840
<i>"Ack! My handlebars are bent!"</i>

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:09.780
<i>"What should we do?"</i>

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:17.350
<b>Riding Comfortably: Maintenance Methods</b>

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:12.640
<i>This time we'll learn</i>

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:16.450
<i>maintenance methods that should be 
performed before riding your bike.</i>

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:21.220
What kind of maintenance 
do road bikes require?

00:22:21.220 --> 00:22:25.590
There are a few things you should 
check before riding your bike.

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:27.610
<b>Y's Road Ochanomizu
Manager Yamada Yunosuke-san</b>

00:22:25.590 --> 00:22:26.470
Before riding your bike?

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:29.660
That's right. The first is 
checking your air pressure.

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:29.660
<b>1: Check air pressure</b>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:34.790
Your tires will lose air pressure over 
time even if you don't ride your bike,

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:38.000
<b>Always touch your tires before riding to check the air pressure</b>

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:38.660
so you should touch them to check their 
pressure before riding your bike.

00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:40.120
Got it.

00:22:40.120 --> 00:22:41.170
Then there's the second point.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:44.100
Check to see if your handlebars are secure.

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>2: Check if handlebars are secure</b>

00:22:44.100 --> 00:22:45.000
Secure?

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:45.460
That's right.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:57.180
<b>Apply force vertically and horizontally to check for bending</b>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:48.470
First, apply vertical force to the handlebars.

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:50.470
Next, try twisting them right and left.

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:54.750
If they're not securely fixed, it 
can lead to bending or accidents,

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:56.440
so it's important to check if they're secure.

00:22:56.440 --> 00:22:57.180
Got it.

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:58.180
Then there's the third point.

00:22:58.180 --> 00:22:58.660
Okay.

00:22:58.660 --> 00:23:00.460
You'll want to check your saddle.

00:22:58.660 --> 00:23:01.230
<b>3: Check if saddle is secure</b>

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:00.760
Okay.

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.410
Grip the saddle and apply force 
vertically and horizontally.

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:08.360
<b>Apply force vertically and horizontally and listen for strange noises</b>

00:23:04.410 --> 00:23:08.360
If you hear any strange crackling noises, 
you'll want to check your torque.

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:10.790
Finally, you'll want to check the chain.

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.320
<b>4: Check chain</b>

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:11.320
The chain.

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:11.320
Okay.

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:13.240
If you don't have enough lubricating oil,

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:16.620
<b>Without sufficient oil, the metal pieces will rub together and create noise</b>

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:16.620
the metal pieces will rub 
together and create noises.

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:19.200
If you turn the pedals and 
hear a jingling noise,

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:25.250
<b>If turning the pedals causes strange noises, add lubricating oil</b>

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.450
you may not have enough oil.

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:21.150
That's not good?

00:23:21.150 --> 00:23:24.260
So you'll want to add more.

00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:29.220
If you do what you can on a regular basis,
your bicycle will last longer,

00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Next Time
"Correct Riding Posture"</b>

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:29.880
Okay.

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:31.900
so I recommend performing maintenance regularly.

00:23:31.900 --> 00:23:33.610
You're right. We have to 
take good care of them.

00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:35.010
Yeah.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time
"All Together!"</b>
